Applied CLT by taking multiple random samples from Black Friday sales data, demonstrating that the sample means approached a normal distribution, even though the original data was skewed. Used bootstrapping & CLT to calculate 95% confidence intervals for average spending across different customer segments, improving decision-making accuracy.
Demonstrated that increasing sample sizes reduced standard error and CL overlap, leading to more reliable sales predictions, helping Walmart optimize inventory and promotional strategies.
Found that male customers spent 7% more than female customers on average, with confidence intervals validating this insight for targeted marketing. Suggested targeted marketing campaigns based on spending behavior and confidence intervals, potentially leading to a 10-15% improvement in campaign effectiveness during Black Friday sales.
